<speak>I'm comfortable, thank you. I brought a glass of water in before the call, so I'm all right. This is already much easier than trying to talk while walking between rooms. My wife often reminds me that a telephone appointment is still an appointment, even if nobody can see whether I'm sitting properly. She says I sound distracted when I'm moving about. Today I've stayed in one place, and I can see why she keeps telling me that.</speak>